 {'chainIds':[4217],'lens':'L2','check':'A credit word of 2^64 or more for the PoolManager makes every zero crossing SSTORE halt with fatal error invalid storage credits state (accounting.rs u64::from_word). Can an ordinary account put the PoolManager in that state, or set its credit mode or budget, so that its writes fail?',
  'result':'No. Every writer of the credit word stores a u64: the SSTORE hook writes U256::from(credit) after saturating_add or a decrement, and StorageCreditDeltas adds with saturating_add for DEX makers. set_mode and set_budget write only the caller own transient state (write_mode_with_budget(msg_sender)), and with_budget and track_minted_credits are used with the DEX or channel reserve address itself as owner. The PoolManager has no call to the credit precompile. The 2^64 run shows only what a state override can do.','source':SCM},
